                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Delicious 14: Emily's Christmas Carol[/b] (Time Management) \n[i]Steam copy provided for Curator review[/i]\n\n[i]An enchanting tale filled with the magic of Christmas[/i]\n\nOptions include separate sliders for Music and Sound, Full-screen or Windowed, Show Game Hints and choice of Difficulty\n\nThe Delicious games always have an optional tutorial, but there is also a 'How to Play\" area in the Settings section if you need it.\n\n[b]Story:[/b]\n\nThe whole family packs up for a trip on the Miracle Express for the Christmas adventure of a lifetime!\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1934453772\nFor those who are new to the franchise, starting at #4, [i]Emily's Taste of Fame[/i], these games are heavily story-driven dash-type time management games, with endearing characters and great gameplay.  \n\nThe story is excellent and the characters are so distinctive that every one of them is memorable.  I was incredibly impressed with how well the devs managed the mannerisms of the children... From temper tantrums to angelic innocence and everything in between, they captured it all beautifully.\n\n[b]Gameplay[/b]:\n\nEach level will present you with a challenge in addition to the usual of delivering food, etc. to customers, and each challenge completed will earn you a diamond, as will completing the Challenge levels.  [b]Diamonds[/b] are used to invite people an in-game event.\n\nEach of the six locations has upgrades that you can buy with the money that you earn from, per usual, but you can also tailor the menu to your play style.  New items to sell will unlock as you play, and then you can choose things like, \"Do I want the drinks to fill faster, or do I want them to be spill-proof?\"  Another example:\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1934453489\nIt seems like the third option would be a no-brainer since it's faster AND makes more money, but it's also a little more complex to put together!\n[list]\n[*]61 story levels + 30 bonus levels for a total of [b]91[/b] challenges/levels to play\n[*]21 in-game and Steam [b]Achievements[/b] (some which you'll really have to work for!)\n[/list]\nThere are [b]secrets[/b] scattered across the maps/levels to keep an eye out for, and a way to turn your customers into reindeer for a level.  I laughed like crazy when I found it! lol~\n\n[b]Sights & Sounds[/b]:\n\nThe graphics this time around are simply stunning.  It also sounds like they've gotten a full orchestra to do their music, and the result is just beautiful.  It's still very \"Emily\", but not the same-old, same-old that you might expect after 14 games.\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1934455961\n[b]Verdict[/b]:\n\nI've played and loved every Emily game since [i]Taste of Fame[/i], and in my opinion, this is the best of the best.  Best graphics, best soundtrack, best storyline, best locations, best gameplay... The only negative is that 'Normal' mode is too easy.  I didn't have to replay any levels until late LATE in the game, but then, I'm an experienced player!  The beauty is that if you find Normal mode too easy, you can always switch to Expert!\n\nOverall, absolutely delightful, and absolutely recommended!!",
